@page "/"

<PageTitle>AspireDEX</PageTitle>

<div class="px-4 py-5">
    <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold">AspireDEX</h1>
    <p class="col-md-8 fs-5 text-muted">
        A decentralized exchange built on .NET Aspire, ASP.NET Core and Solidity — a Uniswap V2-style
        AMM (Factory / Pair / Router) plus a lending protocol (LendingPool, InterestRateModel,
        LiquidationEngine, OracleHub, RiskEngine) sharing the same on-chain deployment.
    </p>

    <div class="row g-4 mt-2">
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card h-100">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h5 class="card-title">Pools</h5>
                    <p class="card-text text-muted">Browse every liquidity pool with live on-chain reserves.</p>
                    <a href="/pools" class="btn btn-outline-primary">View pools</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card h-100">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h5 class="card-title">Swap</h5>
                    <p class="card-text text-muted">Get a live quote from the Router and execute a token swap.</p>
                    <a href="/swap" class="btn btn-outline-primary">Swap tokens</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card h-100">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h5 class="card-title">Liquidity</h5>
                    <p class="card-text text-muted">Add or remove liquidity for any token pair.</p>
                    <a href="/liquidity" class="btn btn-outline-primary">Manage liquidity</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="alert alert-warning mt-5">
        <strong>Demo architecture note:</strong> write operations (swap, add/remove liquidity) are signed
        by a single operator account configured on the API service, not by each visitor's own wallet.
        Client-side wallet signing (MetaMask / WalletConnect) is on the roadmap — see the README.
    </div>
</div>
